    "display_title": "feat(formation): the native walk reads and writes the unit store",
    "event": "pull_request",
    "head_branch": "feature/unit-store-native-walk",
    "head_commit_message": "feat(formation): the native walk reads and writes the unit store\n\nSpec 35 step 4c. BodyField.walk no longer takes each unit's motion and\nframe from GDScript: it reads the bearing, rank and column from the\nstore's columns and the turn rate, backward pace and footprint from\nthe unit's record (the paces now enrolled once with it), and writes\nwhere each unit ends and looks into its loose entry's columns there,\nas ScrumWalkField's write-back did. The facing gathers from the store\nas the walk left it.\n\nTests: test_body_field.gd checks the paces in the record on the field\n(red on the 4b library); the walk parity tests run unchanged through\nthe new path.\n\nWaived-by: Decision 142\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YWpV2AHWr3d2v4fKRki8G7",
